            0.32,
            0.097,
            0.399,
            0.134
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Is air matter?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.204,
            0.145,
            0.391,
            0.291
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 3,
              "bbox": [
                0.204,
                0.145,
                0.391,
                0.291
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_15_image_3.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.452,
            0.084,
            0.884,
            0.145
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can all the materials around us be considered as different examples of matter? Discuss with your friends."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.409,
            0.146,
            0.883,
            0.186
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For example, water is matter, sand and pebbles are matter and so is the cup."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.409,
            0.186,
            0.882,
            0.227
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Materials are types of matter used in the creation or making of objects."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.362,
            0.227,
            0.884,
            0.309
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We learnt that materials look different and behave differently. We grouped materials on the basis of similarities or differences in their properties."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.308,
            0.884,
            0.454
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We find grouping useful as it helps us study and observe patterns in the properties of things. Humans have been classifying not only things, but also rocks, plants and animals. We have learnt about the classification of the living world in the chapter ‘Diversity in the Living World’. Just like in the living world, classification of the non-living world is also done on the basis of their properties."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.287,
            0.478,
            0.36,
            0.526
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.287,
                0.478,
                0.36,
                0.526
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_15_image_9.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.27,
            0.529,
            0.378,
            0.573
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think it over!",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.396,
            0.493,
            0.849,
            0.558
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can you think about what changes the invention of plastic brought to humans? Is it a boon or a bane?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.311,
            0.575,
            0.379,
            0.62
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 12,
              "bbox": [
                0.311,
                0.575,
                0.379,
                0.62
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_15_image_12.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.272,
            0.651,
            0.47,
            0.724
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have explored and understood the various properties of materials."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.556,
            0.609,
            0.829,
            0.702
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Yes! But most of the materials that we see today would have also existed earlier. I am curious to know how people classified them then."
            }
          ]
        },
